SUMMARY:Battman v1.1.0
DESCRIPTION:Battman 1.1.0 | TrollStore\n\n## Battman 1.1.0\n\nIn this versi
 on\, I have finally put something in the 'Analytics' page\, added native p
 lug-in support\, and fixed a bunch of bugs.\n\n**PLEASE LET ME KNOW** when
  you want any new features or find any bugs. You can create a [GitHub issu
 e](https://github.com/Torrekie/Battman/issues/new) to describe them\, espe
 cially when something behaves differently on your device.\n\n- Implemented
  the 'Analytics' page with cards that you can add\, remove\, resize and re
 arrange ([#53](https://github.com/Torrekie/Battman/pull/53)).\n- Added ten
  Analytics cards: live readings\, capacity observations\, cell voltages\, 
 charging sessions\, battery discharge\, connection and charging states\, p
 ower readings\, time by battery level\, charging comparison\, and discharg
 e rhythm. Graphs include capacity history and comparisons of complete 20% 
 to 80% charging sessions\; available readings depend on your device and it
 s recorded history.\n- Added native plug-in support\, including `.battman`
  import\, plug-in management\, diagnostics and recovery mode. Third-party 
 plug-ins require your approval\, and changes take effect after restarting 
 Battman ([#53](https://github.com/Torrekie/Battman/pull/53)).\n- Added the
  public Plugin SDK and plug-in example sources for developers ([#53](https
 ://github.com/Torrekie/Battman/pull/53)). Charge Gauge is provided as a **
 source example**\, not as a shipped production plug-in.\n- Added a 'Temper
 ature Unit' option: System\, Celsius\, or Fahrenheit ([#43](https://github
 .com/Torrekie/Battman/issues/43)).\n- Added `zh_TW` localization and docum
 entation ([#35](https://github.com/Torrekie/Battman/pull/35)).\n- Added 'E
 xport Powerlog' to the charging graph. Long-press the graph to export the 
 available system battery log.\n- Improved charging-limit settings\, daemon
  connections and charging controls\; unavailable or invalid battery readin
 gs now have clearer explanations ([#54](https://github.com/Torrekie/Battma
 n/pull/54)).\n- Fixed potential deadlocks in battery-s
URL:https://raynmahbub.github.io/OmniSource/feeds/battman.json
END:VEVENT
